cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this study or its code, please cite it as below."
title: "RS Corridor Flood Watch: flood-potential thresholds (EDI, API) for the BR-116, BR-386 and BR-290 corridors, Rio Grande do Sul, Brazil"
type: software
version: "1.1.0"
# TODO(author): set to the day the v1.1 release is published, if it is not this one.
date-released: 2026-11-28
authors:
  - family-names: Andrade
    given-names: Valkiria
    # TODO(author): add your ORCID here, e.g. orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
license: MIT
# Concept DOI: always resolves to the latest version (v1.0 is 10.5281/zenodo.24508672).
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24508671"
repository-code: "https://github.com/valkiriaandrade/rs-corridor-flood-watch"
url: "https://rs-corridor-flood-watch.streamlit.app/"
abstract: >-
  Independent study that calibrates and validates, out of sample and against S2iD municipal flood records, flood-potential
  thresholds based on the Effective Drought Index (EDI) and the Antecedent Precipitation Index (API) computed on upstream-basin
  MERGE rainfall, and applies the frozen rules to ECMWF and GFS deterministic forecasts and to the ECMWF ENS and GEFS
  ensembles, with continuous verification of the forecast levels. Pre-registered protocol in docs/protocol.md, including
  the supplementary analyses (forecast-level hindcast, bias correction, GloFAS benchmark, soil moisture); negative results
  are reported. Not an official warning.
keywords:
  - flood
  - effective drought index
  - antecedent precipitation index
  - forecast verification
  - ensemble forecasts
  - GloFAS
  - Rio Grande do Sul
  - S2iD
